/**
 * @defgroup Foundation_Workflows_Configure Configure
 * @ingroup Foundation_Workflows_Configuration
 * @brief Create or update the CMake cache for a preset.
 *
 * Configuration is the only workflow that accepts arbitrary CMake cache
 * overrides. Those values remain in `build/<preset>/CMakeCache.txt` and are
 * reused by later build, test, install, and export operations.
 *
 * Internally, the scripts run `cmake --preset <preset>`, optionally add
 * `--fresh`, and forward caller-supplied CMake arguments. The preset determines
 * the binary directory, generator, compiler/toolchain, architecture, and target
 * identity. Configuration generates build-system files but does not compile,
 * test, install, or export Foundation.
 *
 * @section FoundationWorkflowConfigureBash Bash
 *
 * @code{bash}
 * ./scripts/configure.sh <preset> [--fresh] [-- <cmake arguments>]
 *
 * ./scripts/configure.sh macos_arm64 --fresh
 * ./scripts/configure.sh stm32f407_armgcc_cortex_m4f_hard --fresh -- \
 *     -DFOUNDATION_ARM_TOOLCHAIN_ROOT=/opt/arm-gnu-toolchain \
 *     -DFOUNDATION_ARM_SYSROOT=/opt/arm-none-eabi
 * ./scripts/configure.sh atmega328p_avrgcc_avr5 --fresh -- \
 *     -DFOUNDATION_AVR_TOOLCHAIN_ROOT=/opt/avr-gcc
 * @endcode
 *
 * `--fresh` asks CMake to discard the existing cache before configuration.
 * Arguments after `--` are forwarded directly to `cmake --preset`.
 *
 * @section FoundationWorkflowConfigurePowerShell PowerShell
 *
 * @code{powershell}
 * ./scripts/configure.ps1 <preset> [-Fresh] [-CMakeArguments <arguments>]
 *
 * ./scripts/configure.ps1 arm_none_eabi_cortex_m4f_hard `
 *     -Fresh `
 *     -CMakeArguments "-DFOUNDATION_ARM_SYSROOT=C:/arm/sysroot"
 * @endcode
 *
 * PowerShell collects all remaining arguments in `CMakeArguments`. Quote an
 * argument when its value contains spaces. Bash requires the `--` separator so
 * script options and CMake options cannot be confused.
 *
 * @section FoundationWorkflowConfigureFresh When to Use Fresh
 *
 * Use fresh configuration when:
 *
 * - changing generator, compiler, toolchain file, sysroot, CPU, FPU, or ABI;
 * - preparing a release/export after development or testing overrides;
 * - switching a cache from a full build to a reduced feature set;
 * - diagnosing a result that may depend on stale cache state.
 *
 * Without the fresh option, CMake updates the existing cache. This is faster
 * for normal source edits and preserves explicit feature selections. Fresh
 * configuration removes only the CMake cache/build-system state managed by
 * CMake; use @ref Foundation_Workflows_Clean when the entire build tree should
 * be removed.
 *
 * @section FoundationWorkflowConfigureOptions Foundation Options
 *
 * The main workflow options are:
 *
 * | Option | Default | Effect |
 * | --- | --- | --- |
 * | `FOUNDATION_FULL_BUILD` | `OFF` | Requests the complete module selection. |
 * | `FOUNDATION_DOCS` | `OFF` | Adds the Doxygen `docs` target. |
 * | `FOUNDATION_TESTING` | `OFF` | Enables CTest integration. |
 * | `FOUNDATION_EXAMPLES` | `OFF` | Builds repository examples. |
 * | `FOUNDATION_COVERAGE` | `OFF` | Adds host coverage flags. |
 * | `FOUNDATION_MATH` | `ON` | Includes Math and its selected submodules. |
 * | `FOUNDATION_TYPE_TRAITS` | `ON` | Includes TypeTraits. |
 * | `FOUNDATION_CONTAINERS` | `ON` | Includes Containers. |
 * | `FOUNDATION_SCHEDULING` | `ON` | Includes Scheduling. |
 * | `FOUNDATION_TIME` | `ON` | Includes Time and its selected submodules. |
 * | `FOUNDATION_FUNCTIONAL` | `ON` | Includes Functional. |
 * | `FOUNDATION_UTILS` | `ON` | Includes Utils. |
 *
 * Math, Time, Matrix, and Functional expose additional submodule options in
 * their `CMakeOptions.cmake` files. When a parent is disabled, its child code is
 * not added even if a child cache option remains `ON`.
 *
 * Target presets intentionally leave module options in the CMake cache. This
 * allows a caller to configure a custom feature set once and reuse it for both
 * Debug and Release. Leave `FOUNDATION_FULL_BUILD=OFF` when disabling individual
 * modules; setting it to `ON` explicitly enables the complete module set.
 * Do not override target invariants such as `FOUNDATION_PLATFORM`, CPU, FPU,
 * architecture, or ABI merely to reuse a preset name. Add a new preset/profile
 * when the produced binary has a different compatibility identity.
 *
 * @section FoundationWorkflowConfigureInspect Inspecting the Result
 *
 * Review the configure summary for system, processor, C/C++ compiler, compiler
 * ID, and enabled Foundation features. Important cached values can also be
 * inspected with:
 *
 * @code{bash}
 * cmake -N -LA build/<preset>
 * grep -E "FOUNDATION_|CMAKE_(CXX_COMPILER|SYSTEM_PROCESSOR)" \
 *     build/<preset>/CMakeCache.txt
 * @endcode
 *
 * A successful configure proves that CMake accepted the environment; it does
 * not prove that all source files compile or that the target runtime is complete.
 */
